{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1514949-alternate-systems","id":1514949,"title":"Alternate systems?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-14T06:05:49-07:00","id":1514949,"title":"Alternate systems?","content":"I have some friends who are interested in the setting but turned off by how rules-heavy the system is; core and Essence both. They prefer faster, simpler, more narrative systems, like Dungeon World. I don't know a lot of game systems, so I'm wondering what alternate system you'd use to port the setting over to as much as possible while still aiming for their play sensibilities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T09:09:50-07:00","id":1514965,"title":"","content":"Godbound might be an idea. Its an OSR system and is similar in concept","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Avatar by Raven &amp; Blue Jay.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/663-aleks","name":"Aleks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar663_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T12:37:45-07:00","id":1515001,"title":"","content":"Gods of the Fall by Monte Cook Games is a Cypher System book that might be a decent rules light option. It has its own setting you could use (it has a similar vibe), but I also think you could convert without too much trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T14:31:22-07:00","id":1515019,"title":"","content":"There are a few Fate hacks out there you could try out, and at least one Cortex hack? I can't make any statements as to their quality, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T18:29:52-07:00","id":1515042,"title":"","content":"so if you weren't a backer for it, exalted essence came out literally today. Reading through this guy makes the game refreshingly simple. Feels like going from dnd 3.5 to 5th to be honest. One of the most infuriating things is convincing people that exalted's setting is worth the crunch and i feel essence might be able to take a bit of the sting out of that crunch","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8897-joshopotamus","name":"joshopotamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T20:28:55-07:00","id":1515055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>joshopotamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1514949-alternate-systems?p=1515042#post1515042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted Essence came out literally today.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did, and that was the version I pitched. They still found it overwhelming. I do kind of wonder if that was because I was using the backer document, which made the read an utter slog due to lack of formatting and inserts and stuff to break up the monotony; but alas, the first impression has been made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T04:37:24-07:00","id":1515096,"title":"","content":"There's a few alternate systems that have been made over the last decade called Quixalted/Qwixalted made by various people. There's about...five or so different version of it now, and one of them is explicitly rules lite called 'True Essence'. <br /> <br /> I'd try repitching the new Essence to them but just keep it focused on what you guys want to do - that'll usually just mean you pick one Exalt type. If you're a new player, you'll definitely get overwhelmed by the amount of player options and their permutations available unless you are told explicitly you're just going to be doing one sort of Exalt in my experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T06:51:56-07:00","id":1515656,"title":"","content":"I like the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28047-lewisdavis","name":"LewisDavis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T22:49:26-07:00","id":1515722,"title":"","content":"just for the love of god, dont make it based off 5e. Im seeing people homebrew so many other good systems into 5e and this dumbing down of the hobby has made me commit to not run 5e for awhile","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8897-joshopotamus","name":"joshopotamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T21:06:04-07:00","id":1515821,"title":"","content":"I don't know which game's fifth edition you're talking about here, but could we please agree that there's no need to gatekeep the hobby, and just let people like the games they like? I don't feel like anyone has anything to prove, at least not as far as what specific rules we like to use to pretend to be anime protagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T02:07:32-07:00","id":1515833,"title":"","content":"D&amp;D 5e is the main thing they're mentioning. And I think it's less a gatekeep thing and that we're kind of at a point that I think the need to convert things in it is outright harmful for the hobby. Moslty in that a lot of perfectly good game concepts don't quite mesh with its mechancis and are a lot is lost to contort them to fit 5e rather than often what I think is some other system, either existing or custom, to suit the needs and goals of game creators and homebreweres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T02:32:21-07:00","id":1515837,"title":"","content":"As a matter of personal taste, I agree that I'd rather steer away from d20 / DND 5E conversions. Cypher was a fun time for awhile, but certain experiences have kinda soured interest in anything that smells like the usual d20 core.<br /> <br /> Savage Worlds has always been a middle-ground system I'll champion, admitted nostalgia bias. Enough rules for satisfying crunch and tactical diversity, but not so much it's unwieldy or overwhelming. Though it doesn't strike me as a great platform for Exalted on the surface level, their Rifts adaptation has set a lot of interesting precedents that could inspire a satisfying port.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2394-grifnir","name":"Grifnir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T05:05:07-07:00","id":1519409,"title":"","content":"The Genesys System (originally developed for the latest Star Wars RPG) isn't exactly rules-lite, but I think it's worth mentioning here. It is definitely less rules-overwhelming than Exalted, in the way I'd guess your players are finding objectionable. It's organized more like a traditional D&amp;D-style RPG, but between the Charm-adjacent power trees and the dice pool mechanics, I think it captures some of the vibe of Exalted without being quite so extra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}